NOTES TO SLEF

1. The model is quite close the POINTNET architecture described in the original paper.
  - It has Multi-resolution grouping (MRG) which combines information summarized from the previous level used to construct the information in the smaller subregion.
  

  - Random input dropout
  - T-Net for learning transformations. This is part of the original PointNet architecture
  - The implemented POINTNET model includes a random and farthest point sampling (FPS) option. 
    - The idea behind this is FPS might pick only outlier points and not focus on the object of interest
    - The amount of FPS vs. random sampling is learned using a neural network
  -